## LangWatch changes trace transport and repairs ingestion fidelity

Source: LangWatch — https://github.com/langwatch/langwatch/releases/tag/langwatch%40v3.21.0
Published: 2026-10-21
Channel: github

LangWatch 3.21.0 makes gzipped OTLP/protobuf the default trace transport across its SDKs. The October 21 application release also adds decoding based on compression magic bytes, including zstd or gzip bodies with an incorrect Content-Encoding header. These changes concern the format and acceptance of telemetry at the ingestion boundary; the notes do not establish a measured bandwidth reduction or guarantee that every intermediary supports the new defaults.

Several fixes address what survives ingestion and appears in analysis. OTLP/JSON spans can omit default-valued link or event fields. Claude SDK and API OpenTelemetry traces receive fixes covering usage counted once, large attributes, tool output and cache pricing. Platform metrics are routed through the OpenTelemetry facade so the OTLP push includes them. Bounded error-cause summaries aim to keep request errors from being dropped by Loki.

The release also exposes queue labels and age gauges and supports redriving or discarding more than 2,000 dead-letter groups at once. Together these changes make transport correctness and recovery visibility worth testing together. SDK, application, MCP and Helm tags overlap this release; they should not be counted as separate independent improvements.

Why it matters: Verify compressed ingestion and retained usage fields through the actual proxy path, then confirm queue and dead-letter recovery signals reach monitoring.

